# Creating our non-profit YouTube account

1. The Starting Point. The Parish Administrator should go to the following link to begin the application: [google.com/nonprofits](https://www.google.com/nonprofits/). Crucial: Sign in with a church-owned Google account (e.g., office@stmarysbonita.org or a dedicated stmarysbonita@gmail.com). Do not use a personal account, as this person becomes the "Primary Owner."

2. Information to Gather. The administrator will need the following details ready to enter into the portal:

- Employer Identification Number (EIN): The church’s 9-digit Federal Tax ID.
- Official Legal Name: Must match the IRS records exactly.
- Physical Address: Must match the address on official tax documents.
- Church Website URL: Ensure the website footer displays the church’s legal name and EIN.
3. Required Documentation (Group Exemption). Because most Episcopal churches do not have an individual IRS 501(c)(3) letter, Google's verification partner (Goodstack) will require proof of "Group Exemption." Please have the following PDFs ready:

- The Group Exemption Letter: A copy of the IRS letter issued to the National Episcopal Church (DFMS) or the Diocese of Southwest Florida confirming the group tax-exempt status.
- Proof of Affiliation: A recent page from the Official Episcopal Church Directory (Red Book) showing St. Mary’s, Bonita Springs, as an active parish in good standing.
- Bank-Issued Document: A PDF of a recent church bank statement (financial figures can be redacted) that shows the Church’s Legal Name and Address. This verifies the organization is currently active.
- EIN Verification Letter (Optional but Recommended): The original CP575 or LTR 147C letter from the IRS (the document that originally assigned the EIN).

4. The Verification Timeline

- Submission: Once the form is submitted, the application goes to Goodstack.
- Email Monitoring: The administrator should watch for emails from verifications@mail.goodstack.org. They may ask for a "Letter of Authorization" signed by the Rector.
- Approval: Verification usually takes 2–14 business days.

5. Final Step: Product Activation

- Once approved, the administrator must log back into the Google for Nonprofits dashboard to officially "Activate" the YouTube Nonprofit Program.
- Required Info: They will ask for the YouTube Channel ID: UCeeFfhMcJa1kjtfZAGskOCA
- Note to Administrator: All documents must be uploaded as original electronic PDFs. Scanned copies or photos of documents are often rejected by the automated verification system.

