To ensure the church is fully protected, you will use a feature called "YouTube Studio Permissions." This is the modern, secure way to add "keys" to the account without sharing the master password.

Because you are setting this up as a Brand Account (which is a requirement for YouTube Nonprofit), you can have multiple people log in with their own personal Google accounts to manage the church's channel.

## Step-by-Step: Adding Managers

- Sign In: Log in to the new church account and go to [studio.youtube.com](https://studio.youtube.com).
- Open Settings: On the left-hand menu, click the Settings (gear icon) at the very bottom.
- Permissions: Click the Permissions tab on the left.
- Invite: Click the blue Invite button at the top right.
- Enter Details:
- Email: Enter the personal email address of the person you want to add (e.g., the Rector or Parish Admin).
- Access: Select Manager.
- Save: Click Done and then Save.
- Note: YouTube will ask you to verify your identity (usually via a code to the master account's phone) before it saves the changes.

## Understanding the Roles (Which to Choose?)

For the best protection of St. Mary’s, I recommend the following "Rule of Three":

- Manager (Highest Level): Give this to yourself and the Rector. Capabilities: Can add/remove other managers, upload/delete videos, and change all channel details.
- Editor (Middle Level): Give this to reliable volunteers. Capabilities: Can upload videos and edit descriptions, but cannot add/remove users or delete the channel.
- Viewer (Lowest Level): Give this to a church board member who wants to see the "Analytics" (how many people are watching) but shouldn't be able to change anything.

## The "Primary Owner" Safety Net

- The email address the Parish Administrator uses to create the account will be the Primary Owner.
- Wait Period: If you ever need to change the "Primary Owner" (for example, if the church office changes its main email address), YouTube has a 7-day security delay.
- The Benefit: This delay prevents a hacker from instantly stealing the channel, as the existing owner will receive an alert and can stop the transfer.

## Final "Future-Proofing" Tip

- Every January, make it a habit to open this Permissions menu. If a volunteer has moved away or a staff member has retired, remove their access immediately. This keeps the "digital doors" of St. Mary's locked and secure.
